// Type-checking for TEST files. Fixes #952.
//
// Before this, tsconfig.app.json EXCLUDED every *.test.ts(x), and the root
// referenced only app + node — so test files were type-checked by nothing.
// 250 latent errors had accumulated across 80 files, including nine
// `@ts-expect-error` directives that were already suppressing nothing: guards
// someone wrote that had silently stopped guarding.
//
// This project checks the test files. The `exclude` list below was the DEBT:
// every file in it was known-bad and skipped, and it only ever shrank.
//
// IT IS NOW EMPTY. Every test file under `src` is type-checked — with no
// `@ts-nocheck`, no `as unknown as` added, and no compiler option softened.
//
// The point was the asymmetry. A NEW test file was checked immediately — it
// could not join the list, so no new debt could be added — while the existing
// files were burned down a few at a time.
//
// This file still earns its keep for `types`: test files need `node` and
// `jest-axe`, which the app build does not. Folding it into tsconfig.app.json
// (and dropping that file's `src/**/*.test.*` exclude) means moving those two
// into the app's own `types` first, so it is left as its own change.
//
// Verified real: adding a new test file with a type error fails
// `npm --prefix web run typecheck`. A green `tsc -b` here is not vacuous.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.app.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.test.tsbuildinfo",
    "types": [
      "vite/client",
      "vitest/globals",
      "node",
      "jest-axe"
    ]
  },
  "include": [
    "src"
  ],
  "exclude": []
}
